# Conventional Commits

When the user asks you to commit changes, always write the commit message using the [Conventional Commits](https://www.conventionalcommits.org/) format:

```
<type>(<scope>): <description>
```

## Types

| Type | Use when |
|------|----------|
| `feat` | A new feature or user-facing capability |
| `fix` | A bug fix |
| `docs` | Documentation only |
| `style` | Formatting, whitespace — no logic change |
| `refactor` | Code change that is neither a fix nor a feature |
| `perf` | Performance improvement |
| `test` | Adding or updating tests |
| `chore` | Build, CI, deps, tooling — no production code change |

## Rules

- **Scope** (optional but preferred): short area name, e.g. `dmx`, `docs`, `frontend`, `party-mode`
- **Description**: imperative mood, lowercase, no trailing period — e.g. `add emergency stop button`, not `Added emergency stop button.`
- **One line** for simple changes; add a body only when the why is not obvious from the subject
- Pick the type that best matches the *primary intent* of the change

## Examples

```
feat(dmx): add emergency stop button
fix(frontend): prevent universe grid scroll jump on resize
docs: update raspberry pi installation guide
refactor(dmx): extract universe channel mapping into hook
chore: bump wails to v2.9.1
```

```
// ❌ BAD
updated docs
Add multi-universe DMX support
feat: stuff

// ✅ GOOD
docs: update universe and live-mode guides
feat(dmx): add multi-universe support up to 4 universes
```
